          <div class="charge-col">
            <h1>Arthur Grosvenor Daniells &mdash;<br><em>The President Who Signed Away the Church</em></h1>
            <p class="charge-sub">
              Arthur G. Daniells was the <strong style="color:var(--gold-soft);">General Conference President of the Seventh-day Adventist denomination</strong> at the time of the April 15, 1904 incorporation. As the highest authority in the organization, he did not merely witness or endorse the signing — he orchestrated it. His name appears first among the Takoma Park signatories. He had read Ellen White's Letter 242 (October 1903). He had heard her warnings against centralization. He signed anyway.
            </p>
            <div class="fact-row">
